//~ compile_fail(backend)
//~ error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch

// NEGATIVE (must FAIL to compile): build a lock and throw it away without ever
// taking it. This is pillar 4's asymmetry for `uklock`.
//
// `destroy` accepts only <!idle>, and <idle!> is minted only by `read.release`,
// `write.release` or the named escape `hold.skipped`. So a lock that was created
// and never entered has no way out.
//
// THE C HAS NOTHING TO SAY ABOUT IT, and could not have.
// `uk_rwlock_init_config` on a struct nobody ever locks is correct, silent and
// warning-free; there is no destructor to assert in, because `uklock` has none.
// The mistake is not a memory error, it is a DESIGN error: a lock exists to
// serialize a critical section, so a lock with no critical section means either
// the section was deleted and the lock outlived it, or the section exists and
// somebody forgot to take the lock around it. The second reading is a data race
// that no amount of testing finds.
//
// The legitimate case stays expressible and stays loud. A lock built on a path
// that turns out not to need it says `unikraft/lock:hold.skipped` and compiles —
// `boot_lock.kz` does exactly that, and boots. What this rejects is the SILENT
// version, where the deliberate no-op and the forgotten critical section are
// spelled identically.
//
//     grep -r "lock:hold.skipped"   ->   "which locks do we build and never enter"
//
// EXPECTED: error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch: expected
//           'unikraft.lock:idle' but got 'unikraft.lock:fresh!'
//           for argument 'lock'

// The `unikraft` namespace is declared here, not inherited: koruc's built-in
// alias probes the sibling koru-libs CHECKOUT, so in a worktree this file would
// otherwise compile against main's lifts instead of the ones beside it.
~std/compiler:paths {
    unikraft: {{ ENTRY }}/../..
}

~import unikraft/lock
~import std/io

~unikraft/lock:probe
| ready proof |> unikraft/lock:create(proof.locks)
    | lock guard |> unikraft/lock:destroy(lock: guard)
        |> std/io:print.ln("should never get here")
    | unavailable why |> std/io:print.ln("create failed: {{ why:s }}")
| unsupported why |> std/io:print.ln("uk_rwlock layout refused: {{ why:s }}")
